From d42025414688ea84944f8502153c770196fb2018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:12:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/50] macOS IWA: hide native titlebar buttons in unframed windows

Unframed isolated web apps remove the web app toolbar, but macOS still
creates a titled window in the remote Cocoa app shim. Its native close,
minimize and zoom buttons remain visible over app content. Send the unframed
state to the actual NSWindow, hide or restore its standard buttons, and
remove the caption exclusion from the browser layout.

Covers style-mask changes and permission grant/revoke transitions.
Re-anchored against stock Chromium 160.0.8176.0 (zero downstream browser
context dependencies).

Bug: 482535474
Test: BrowserNativeWidgetWindowTest.UnframedTitlebarButtons (remote_cocoa
      unit test) and the unframed IWA browser test, re-anchored to Chromium
      160 (pending compile/run verification on Chromium 160).
